jobs.description:
Our client is a major player in the logistics sector. They handle road transport, air freight, and sea freight.

The Antwerp branch is responsible for everything related to ocean freight. Around 100 employees work there and give their best every day to provide the highest possible level of service. They are seated in groups of four colleagues at work islands, spread over two floors. The atmosphere on the work floor is calm—sometimes hectic—but very pleasant. There is strong teamwork, and there is certainly room for regular laughter as well.

Every two weeks, a fruit basket is delivered to the departments. In addition, you can work with flexible hours, there are various opportunities for personal development, and subscriptions for the toll tunnel and the water bus are fully reimbursed.

In short: a very attractive employer!

Jobomschrijving


• You are responsible for preparing shipping documentation, Bills of Lading, COO, Insurance certificates, etc.;	
• You check documents and ensure accurate administration;	
• You maintain contacts with shipping agencies, the DHL network, carriers, and customers;	
• You provide excellent customer service and follow-up;	
• You work very accurately and are used to working under time pressure;


• Experience in logistics (preferably in ocean freight)	
• You have strong documentation knowledge;	
• You have good computer skills with basic knowledge of Excel, Word, etc.;	
• You have an excellent command of English (both written and spoken);	
• You are willing to come to the office daily (remote work is not possible);	
• You work accurately and organized and are a team player;	
• You are stress-resistant and can work under time pressure;	
• You communicate easily with colleagues and customers
